<title>USA: Diamond Home Services Q4 net edges higher.</title>
<headline>Diamond Home Services Q4 net edges higher.</headline>
<dateline>WOODSTOCK, Ill. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diamond Home Services Inc said Monday higher sales helped earnings in the fourth quarter rise compared to one year ago.</p>
<p>Net income in the period ended December 31 rose to $2.0 million, or $0.21 a share, from $1.3 million, or $0.21 a share, the company said. The number of weighted average shares increased by 47 percent in the quarter after the company's initial public offer in June 1996.</p>
<p>Sales reached $42.9 million versus $34.9 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Diamond Home Services markets home improvement products.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading off 1/2 Monday at 18-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
